<% @title = "About" %>
<section class="panel about-panel">
  <h1>About HIVEHUB</h1>
  <p>
    I got back into Necromunda with the newest(N26) edition of the game, and like every
    fresh-faced juve stumbling into the underhive I immediately started
    looking for excuses to over-engineer something. HIVEHUB is the result:
    a little tool to make campaign map generation a bit of <em>fun</em> —
    randomly charted hex maps of contested turf, mapped onto the Dominion
    Campaign territories, with just enough grimdark flavour to feel at home
    beneath the hive.

    I say I got <em>back</em> into Necromunda because I actually first played it back in School in the 90s! I couldn't afford the proper box but I dutifully saved my pocket money to buy metal gangs (Van Saar, Escher) and actually mail-ordered just the rulebooks for some tiny sum. Those were the days, chummer. Those were the days.
  </p>
  <p>
    Anyway, the goal here is simple: give Arbitrators a quick way to generate, manage and
    print zone maps for their campaign seasons — who holds what, where the
    no-man's-land lies, and which unlucky stretch of pipework your gang calls
    home. 
    If it saves you a whiteboard and a fistful of sticky notes on game
    night, it's done its job. 
  </p>
  <h2>Development</h2>
  <p>
    Ruby/Sinatra with a sqlite backend. Heavily supported and augmented via github copilot because it can cogitate my ideas into reality much quicker than I can (within reason).
  </p>
  <h2>Suggestions &amp; Bug Reports</h2>
  <p>
    Found a rat in the vents? Got an idea that would make this better? Open
    an issue on the
    <a href="https://github.com/astromoose/hivehub/issues" rel="noopener">GitHub issues page</a>
    — suggestions, silly messages, bug reports and pull requests are all welcome.
  </p>
